UI Components
- Create responsive upload area with drag-and-drop.
- Implement loading states for API calls.
- Display grid and word results efficiently.
- for grid display, use the MultiGridDisplay component with these rules:
Each Letter in Its Own Box

Draw (or imagine) a clear boundary around each letter, so each letter sits in its own square or rectangular “cell.”
No Lines Inside the Boxes

The connecting lines (paths) should never run through the interior of a letter’s box.
Instead, they should go around or between the boxes, keeping the letters fully visible.
Consistent Entry/Exit Points

When you connect two boxes, always enter and exit at the edge or corner that makes sense for the direction you’re moving.
Horizontal: Exit the left box at the right edge, enter the next box at its left edge.
Vertical: Exit the top box at the bottom edge, enter the next box at its top edge.
Diagonal: Decide which diagonal corner to use (for instance, top-left to bottom-right or top-right to bottom-left) and keep that consistent.
Corners vs. Edges

If you’re drawing a diagonal line, use the corner of each box to “turn” or exit.
If you’re drawing a straight line (horizontal or vertical), use the middle of the corresponding edge.
Maintain Spacing

Keep a small gap between the connecting lines and any box corners or edges that aren’t in use, so the path looks intentional rather than cluttered.
Visual Consistency

Apply these rules the same way across all boxes.
This ensures the final layout looks uniform and easy to follow, with lines clearly traveling in logical paths around the letter blocks instead of through them.

API Integration
- Structure OpenAI API calls with proper error handling.
- Implement rate limiting and request queuing.
- Cache results where appropriate.

Performance Optimization
- Minimize client-side processing.
- Use proper loading states during API calls.
- Implement efficient word validation algorithms.

Security
- Validate image uploads server-side.
- Secure API key handling.
- Implement proper CORS and CSP headers.

Follow the project requirements in instructions/instruction.md for specific implementation details.
